.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESM-ADD-BUCKET-TAG 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-esm-add-bucket-tag \- add a tag to a bucket
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli esm add-bucket-tag
.BR \-\-bucket | \-b
.I BUCKET
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.BR \-\-value | \-v
.I VALUE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds a tag (a key/value pair) to a bucket. If a tag with the given key
already exists, its value is overwritten \- so this is the one of the
three that always succeeds, whether or not the key was there before.
.PP
Tags are arbitrary metadata the bucket carries: what a bucket is for,
who owns it, which environment it belongs to. Nothing in euclid
interprets them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-bucket " " \fIBUCKET\fR
Bucket to tag, by name or by Euclid resource name (ERN). Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Tag key. Required.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-value " " \fIVALUE\fR
Tag value. Required.
.PP
The bucket may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The tag was added. No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing or invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or
no such bucket exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm add-bucket-tag \e
    --bucket transfer-server \e
    --key team --value payments
.fi
.RE
.PP
The same command against a bucket in another namespace, which is what a
full ERN is for:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 esm add-bucket-tag \e
    --bucket ern:esm:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:bucket:transfer-server \e
    --key team --value payments
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-set-bucket-tag (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-delete-bucket-tag (1),
.BR euclid-cli-esm-get-bucket-size (1)
